{
  "slug": "perf",
  "name": "Perf",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Structured performance investigation with baselines, profiling, and evidence-backed decisions — run by AI agents inside your editor. `/perf` enforces a rigorous 10-phase methodology derived from recorded real investigation sessions: establish a baseline, identify the breaking point, generate hypotheses, profile, run controlled experiments, measure, document. No random micro-optimizations; every change is baselined, isolated, measured, and either kept or reverted with evidence. Designed to keep the agent honest in a domain where intuition is usually wrong.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **8 skills**, **6 agents** and **1 command**.\n\n- **Skills** (8): `perf-analyzer` (Use when synthesizing perf findings into evidence-backed recommendations and decisions), `perf-baseline-manager` (Use when managing perf baselines, consolidating results, or comparing versions), `perf-benchmarker` (Use when running performance benchmarks, establishing baselines, or validating regressions with sequential runs), `perf-code-paths` (Use when mapping code paths, entrypoints, and likely hot files before profiling), `perf-investigation-logger` (Use when appending structured perf investigation notes and evidence), `perf-profiler` (Use when profiling CPU/memory hot paths, generating flame graphs, or capturing JFR/perf evidence), `perf-theory-gatherer` (Use when generating performance hypotheses backed by git history and code evidence), `perf-theory-tester` (Use when running controlled perf experiments to validate hypotheses)\n- **Agents** (6): `perf-analyzer` (Synthesize perf findings into evidence-backed recommendations and decisions), `perf-code-paths` (Map likely code paths for perf scenarios before profiling), `perf-investigation-logger` (Append structured investigation notes with exact user quotes and rationale), `perf-orchestrator` (Coordinate /perf investigations across all phases, enforcing non-negotiable perf rules), `perf-theory-gatherer` (Generate top performance hypotheses after reviewing git history and current metrics), `perf-theory-tester` (Execute controlled perf experiments, one change at a time, with rollback between runs)\n- **Commands** (1): `perf` (Structured performance investigation with baselines, profiling, and evidence-backed decisions)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install perf@claude-community` from `agent-sh/perf`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 8,
    "agent": 6,
    "command": 1
  },
